There are $\binom{20}{4}=20\cdot19\cdot18\cdot17/24=4845$ equally likely committees. A committee fails the condition exactly when it consists of all boys or all girls. Each case has $\binom{10}{4}=10\cdot9\cdot8\cdot7/24=210$ choices, and the cases are disjoint.

The desired probability is therefore $(4845-2\cdot210)/4845=4425/4845$. Dividing numerator and denominator by 15 gives $295/323$.
Final answer: \dfrac{295}{323}
